{
  "slug": "groq",
  "name": "Groq",
  "tagline": "The premier neocloud for fast inference",
  "description": "Groq is an American AI infrastructure company that pioneered the Language Processing Unit (LPU), a purpose-built inference accelerator, and now operates a global AI inference cloud. Founded in 2016 by former Google engineers led by TPU designer Jonathan Ross, Groq launched the GroqCloud developer platform in 2024 and scaled to 13 data centers across North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific, serving more than six million developers. In December 2025, Groq entered a non-exclusive licensing agreement with NVIDIA under which NVIDIA agreed to pay roughly $20 billion for rights to Groq's inference technology and hired Ross and several senior executives; Groq continued to operate as an independent company. Groq is now focused on building a neocloud for fast, low-cost inference on NVIDIA's accelerated computing alongside its own LPU-derived LPX technology.",
